From 8640915738e575577899fd6dc924ef5d2e420bd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:38:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] text: paint -webkit-text-stroke

Text runs whose style has a non-zero -webkit-text-stroke-width now paint a second run over
the fill, in -webkit-text-stroke-color, using a font instance whose glyphs WebRender
rasterizes as the outline of a stroke of that width (airgap/webrender's FreeType stroker).
Font instances are keyed on the stroke width as well as the painter, and the font services
and paint API now pass whole FontInstanceOptions instead of only their flags so the width
reaches WebRender. The glyph bounds grow by half the stroke width.

Only WebRender's FreeType rasterizer strokes outlines, so on macOS and Windows no stroke is
painted rather than painting filled glyphs in the stroke colour.
https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#the-webkit-text-stroke

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
